<protocol name="resource_efficiency" type="cross_cutting" domain="creative">

## PURPOSE

Work efficiently within execution limits (~30 tool calls per run).

---

## CORE PRINCIPLE

```
[Task] -> [Plan minimum tools] -> [Execute] -> [Verify once] -> [Done]
```

**Anti-pattern:** Tool-call-per-thought, trial-and-error loops.

---

## BATCHING

```
INEFFICIENT:
- image_studio(remove_bg, img1)
- image_studio(remove_bg, img2)
- image_studio(remove_bg, img3)

EFFICIENT:
- image_studio(remove_bg, [img1, img2, img3])
```

---

## NO REDUNDANT CALLS

- Don't re-view same image
- Don't re-load same protocol
- Don't re-verify already-verified output

---

## KNOW WHEN DONE

**Done:** Primary deliverable complete + quality verified.

**Over-engineering:** "Just one more check" / unrequested extras.

---

## APPROACHING LIMITS

1. STOP speculative calls
2. Complete core task
3. Flag gaps: "Did not verify X due to resource constraints"

</protocol>
